The images built from this repository contain third-party software under its own licences; nothing in this repository relicenses it.
For the af3jax image (ports/af3jax/container/Dockerfile), the main components are:
  - AlphaFold 3 source code, v3.1.4 as the sokrypton/alphafold3 JAX fork pins it (Copyright 2024 DeepMind Technologies Limited, and
    the fork's authors): Apache License 2.0. Upstream changed the code licence from CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 to Apache 2.0 on 2026-06-09.
  - The af3_jax optimisation kit, anthropics/uplifting-biomolecular-modeling (Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC): Apache License 2.0,
    with its own NOTICE, kept in the image at /opt/af3jax/ubm.
  - JAX, jaxlib and the jax-rocm7 plugin (Apache License 2.0), and the other Python packages of the kit's lock file, each under its
    own licence.
  - AMD ROCm 7.2.4 libraries (MIT, BSD and other licences, per package) and the rocm/dev-ubuntu-24.04 base image (Ubuntu packages
    under their own licences).
  - CPython 3.12.1 (PSF License), from python-build-standalone.
  - HMMER 3.4 (BSD 3-Clause), with AlphaFold 3's jackhmmer patch.
  - Chemical component data derived from the wwPDB Chemical Component Dictionary (CC0 1.0), built into AlphaFold 3's data files.

The mmseqs2-hip image (ports/mmseqs2-hip/container/Dockerfile), and every image that copies its binary, contains:
  - MMseqs2 (soedinglab/MMseqs2, commit 564f40d8857f4eca4e1dfe100c67c155b1933e70), built from that source by the Dockerfile:
    GNU General Public License v3.0. The corresponding source is the upstream repository at that commit.
  - AMD ROCm 7.2.4's HIP runtime packages and the Ubuntu 24.04 base image (packages under their own licences).

The colabfold image (ports/colabfold/container/Dockerfile) contains, besides that MMseqs2 binary and the ROCm components above:
  - ColabFold 1.6.3 (sokrypton/ColabFold): MIT License; alphafold-colabfold 2.3.20 (AlphaFold 2 code, Copyright DeepMind): Apache 2.0;
    colabfold-binaries 0.1.0 (kalign, hhsearch, under their own licences).
  - JAX, jaxlib and the jax-rocm7 plugin (Apache License 2.0), and the other Python packages of ports/colabfold/environment/requirements.lock,
    each under its own licence.
  - The ColabFold optimisation kit, anthropics/uplifting-biomolecular-modeling (Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC): Apache License 2.0, with
    its own NOTICE, at /opt/colabfold/kit.
  - CPython 3.12.12 (PSF License), from python-build-standalone.
  The AlphaFold 2 model parameters are not included (CC BY 4.0, Google DeepMind): the image reads a copy from outside.

The boltz2 image (ports/boltz2/container/Dockerfile) contains, besides the ROCm components above:
  - Boltz 2.2.1 (jwohlwend/boltz; MIT License), installed from the wheel the optimisation kit ships and pins.
  - PyTorch 2.14.0+rocm7.2 and triton-rocm 3.8.0 (BSD-style licences), which carry their own ROCm 7.2 runtime libraries, and the other
    Python packages of ports/boltz2/environment/requirements.lock, each under its own licence.
  - The Boltz-2 optimisation kit, anthropics/uplifting-biomolecular-modeling (Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC): Apache License 2.0, with
    its own NOTICE, at /opt/boltz2/kit.
  - CPython 3.12.12 (PSF License), from python-build-standalone.
  The Boltz-2 weights are not included (MIT, boltz-community on Hugging Face): `boltz2 fetch-weights` downloads them at the user's request.

The protenix image (ports/protenix/container/Dockerfile) contains, besides ROCm components like those above:
  - Protenix 2.0.0 (bytedance/Protenix, tag v2.0.0, commit 2475421477ab414b571149ad4a875c390ff8a35d; Copyright 2024 ByteDance and/or its
    affiliates), installed from the optimisation kit's own wheel of that release: Apache License 2.0.
  - The Protenix v2 optimisation kit, anthropics/uplifting-biomolecular-modeling (Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC): Apache License 2.0, with
    its own NOTICE and third-party notices (protenix_v2/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md), at /opt/protenix/kit.
  - PyTorch 2.14.0+rocm7.2 (BSD 3-Clause, with the ROCm 7.2 libraries its wheel bundles) and triton-rocm 3.8.0 (MIT), and the other Python
    packages of ports/protenix/environment/requirements.lock, each under its own licence.
  - CPython 3.12.12 (PSF License), from python-build-standalone.
  The Protenix v2 checkpoint and its data caches are not included: `protenix fetch-weights` downloads them at run time.

MODEL PARAMETERS ARE NOT INCLUDED

No image and no file in this repository contains model weights or parameters. The AlphaFold 3 model parameters are available from
Google DeepMind under the AlphaFold 3 Model Parameters Terms of Use, which forbid redistribution: obtain your own copy and keep it
private. The OpenFold3-preview2 weights (Apache 2.0, the OpenFold Consortium) are likewise not included.
